# In a loop, `x instanceof Dog` is false for the shape of a Cat only if the object's prototype link is unchanged since its allocation.
# Out of the compiler's sight, the prototype of one Cat is set to Dog.prototype.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreSiblingPrototypes: the prototype link of an object with the shape of a sibling layout is not checked.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) each result derived from shapes is checked against a walk of the prototype chain that gives up at a trap and runs no code.
# If they disagree, the process crashes.
